      "side": 1,
      "message": "!F0 or F3 only: I think it is the latter, because STM32_RCC_CFGR3_I2C2 exists only for F3.\n\nTalking to Vincent and Alec, there is a catch on Ryu: we need CONFIG_LOW_POWER, but we also want 48Mhz for the slave port, and we can because we disable idle mode when the AP is in S0.\nSo we should leave the ifdef as is. [ugly]",
      "revId": "a249e50cb801d7b11a2050af4e6e3114dee4b5fd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6399ed2_947c4a4f",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/i2c-stm32f0.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-10-30T00:20:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So basically, for Ryu, we define CONFIG_HOSTCMD_I2C_SLAVE_ADDR + CONFIG_LOW_POWER_IDLE and I2C_PORT_EC \u003d\u003d STM32_I2C2_PORT, yet we want to use SCLK for STM32_I2C2_PORT. If that\u0027s the case, I should probably redo this entire change (and move clock configuration to the board-level somehow through a configuration option) because it breaks our assumptions.",
      "parentUuid": "36204e91_5803a125",
      "revId": "a249e50cb801d7b11a2050af4e6e3114dee4b5fd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
